# The whole example as one assembly: the distribution-area frame (its areas, Feeders and ties), the
# boundary model, the substation and feeder frames, then the steady state hypothesis (SSH) of every
# feeder frame.
#
# Each file declares the reference data it uses (base voltages, line impedances, wires, spacings), so
# a file loaded after another that declares the same object restates it.
#
# The order matters in one place: the distribution-area frame, then the boundary nodes, before any
# other frame, because cimtables gives a node with no container the container of the first equipment
# that touches it.

Profile = cim18v17
Authority = https://github.com/PNNL-CIM-Tools/CIMTBL-Models
Model = boundary_example

Import dso_area.cimtbl
Import boundary.cimtbl

Import substation_s1.cimtbl
Import substation_s2.cimtbl

Import feeder_s1_f1.cimtbl
Import feeder_s1_f2.cimtbl
Import feeder_s1_f3.cimtbl
Import feeder_s2_f1.cimtbl
Import feeder_s2_f2.cimtbl

Import ssh_s1_f1.cimtbl
Import ssh_s1_f2.cimtbl
Import ssh_s1_f3.cimtbl
Import ssh_s2_f1.cimtbl
Import ssh_s2_f2.cimtbl
